From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 23:17:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Paint range inputs and select chevrons in accent colours

Read the live value from SpecialElementData::RangeInput and the min and
max attributes. The thumb center travels [left+r, right-r] so the thumb
never overhangs the border box. The filled portion and thumb use the
same accent color the checkbox and radio paint derive (element color,
gray when disabled).

Skipped for multiple and size>1 (inline listboxes). Sized off the box
height, right-aligned, stroked in the element color.

Checkbox, radio and range derive their widget color from the computed
accent-color, falling back to Chrome's default light-mode accent blue on
auto instead of the element text color, which painted black widgets on
most pages. The range track uses the common UA gray.
